questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a Spring Boot batch worker encounters a sudden `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` after processing around 50,000 records. The service utilizes the following implementation:

java
@Service
public class IngestionService {
    @PersistenceContext
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    @Transactional
    public void processBulkRecords(List<RecordDto> incomingRecords) {
        for (int i = 0; i < incomingRecords.size(); i++) {
            RecordEntity entity = RecordEntity.fromDto(incomingRecords.get(i));
            entityManager.persist(entity);
            if (i % 1000 == 0) {
                entityManager.flush();
            }
        }
    }
}


A heap dump analysis shows millions of `RecordEntity` instances remaining strongly reachable despite calling `entityManager.flush()` periodically.
